<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH CHAMPION STAKES RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH CHAMPION STAKES RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>LEOPARDSTOWN, Ireland 1996-09-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the</p>
<p>Irish Champion Stakes, a group one race for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over one and a quarter miles (2.0 kms) on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Timarida	3-1	  (Johnny Murtagh)</p>
<p> 2. Dance Design  9-2	  (Michael Kinane)</p>
<p> 3. Glory of Dancer  10-1    (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>Six ran. Shaamit 5-4 favourite was fourth.</p>
<p>Distances: one and half lengths, a neck.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Aga Khan and trained in Ireland by John</p>
<p>Oxx.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 90,300 pounds ($140,400).</p>
